Package: gnome-shell-extension-lidfx
Version: @VERSION@
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 45), python3
Recommends: python3-numpy, python3-gi, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
Maintainer: Ayush Goyal <126490041+agayushh@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/agayushh/lidfx
License: MIT
Description: fold the GNOME desktop with the laptop lid
 LidFx is a GNOME Shell extension that warps the live wallpaper and
 windows as you close the lid. It reads a lid-angle sensor, dual
 accelerometers, or the display IMU, and falls back to the lid webcam
 on clamshells that have none.
